// Title: Potential ShellDispatch.DLL Functionality Abuse
// Sigma ID: 82343930-652f-43f5-ab70-2ee9fdd6d5e9
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: X__Junior (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-06-20 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth
// Description: Detects potential "ShellDispatch.dll" functionality abuse to execute arbitrary binaries via
//   "ShellExecute"
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.hexacorn.com/blog/2023/06/07/this-lolbin-doesnt-exist/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_rundll32_shelldispatch_potential_abuse.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "RUNDLL32.EXE") and ProcessCommandLine contains "RunDll_ShellExecuteW"
